\cf5 \cb3 validated with holo-omic biomarkers and designed for the specific vul\'ad\
nerabilities of hematology patients. Precision approaches that target\
discrete microbial enzymes, deploy defined microbial consortia, or\
replace protective metabolites offer the dual advantage of mechanistic\
specificity and translatability. If the field adopts standardized multiomic pipelines, trials that embed mechanistic endpoints, and harmo\'ad\
nized safety frameworks for immunocompromised populations, the gut\
microbiome can be transformed from a variable confounder into a\
tractable therapeutic ally that improves the efficacy and tolerability of\
treatments for blood cancers.\
