Chou-Yi Hsu, Ph.D., is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Pharmacy at Chia Nan\
University of Pharmacy and Science, Taiwan. His research interests focus on pharmaco\'ad\
microbiomics, drug metabolism, and personalized medicine strategies in oncology.\
Yasir Qasim Almajidi, Ph.D., is a faculty member in the Department of Pharmaceutics at\
Alnahrain University, Iraq. His research explores novel drug delivery systems and the role\
of the microbiome in modulating pharmacokinetics and therapeutic outcomes.\
Mohammad Abohassan, Ph.D., is a researcher in the Department of Clinical Laboratory\
Sciences at King Khalid University, Saudi Arabia. His work centers on translational med\'ad\
ical research, with a focus on biomarkers and host-microbiome interactions in disease.\
Rushen Gafarov, M.D., is affiliated with the Department of Urology at Samarkand State\
Medical University, Uzbekistan. His clinical and research activities involve urological\
oncology and the systemic implications of the microbiome on cancer therapy.\
Tina Saeed Basunduwah is a medical student at Albatterjee Medical College, Saudi Arabia.\
She is developing her academic interests in hematology-oncology and the emerging field of\
pharmacomicrobiomics.\
Ahmed Hjazi, Ph.D., is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Medical Laboratory\
Sciences at Prince Sattam bin Abdulaziz University, Saudi Arabia. His research focuses on\
clinical diagnostics, molecular medicine, and the interplay between microbiota and cancer\
pathogenesis.\
Vimal Arora, Ph.D., is a scholar at the University Institute of Pharma Sciences, Chandigarh\
University, India. His research encompasses pharmaceutical sciences, with a keen interest\
in drug-microbiome interactions and therapeutic optimization.\
Priya Priyadarshini Nayak, M.D., is a specialist in the Department of Medical Oncology at\
IMS and SUM Hospital, Siksha 'O' Anusandhan University, India. Her clinical research\
focuses on hematologic malignancies and supportive care, including microbiome-based\
interventions.\
Sandeep Kumar Shukla, Ph.D., is a faculty member at the Sharda School of Pharmacy,\
Sharda University, India. His research interests include pharmaceutical biotechnology,\
pharmacokinetics, and the development of microbiome-targeted therapies.\
Karthikeyan Jayabalan, Ph.D., is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Chemistry at\
Sathyabama Institute of Science and Technology, India. His research involves bioorganic\
chemistry and the chemical basis of host-microbe-drug interactions.\
